    "updated_at": "2020-07-03T16:43:08Z",
    "body": "> Both are 1.41.0. I'll happily give more info, too, just let me know, @andytom!\r\n\r\nNo that is enough, the problem should be fixed if you upgrade to a newer version of rust. This feature was added in [`v1.43.0`](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/blob/master/RELEASES.md#version-1430-2020-04-23) so anything more recent than that should work.\r\n\r\n> **Edit:** I'm liking starship, but unfortunately I can't start using it in earnest yet. As soon as I `cd` into (not even `ls`) a folder containing a git repository with on the order of tens of thousands of items (recursively, not directly in that folder), it starts maxing out a CPU core and never seems to finish either. Without starship, just bash, the same operation is practically instananeous. I'll keep it installed, though, for the rustc/cargo version thing.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately that is a know issue at the moment, see #940.",
